This post explores the odds of success when reading confused blessed
remove curse to make both holy and unholy water from uncursed water.
It assumes that you have individually named each flask so it occupies
a different inventory slot, and you are advised of course to drop
other items.  A good result is getting both holy water and unholy
water from the one reading of the scroll.  How many flasks of water
should you have before trying the scroll?

Each uncursed item in inventory has a 25% chance of being blessed and
a 25% chance of being cursed.  A bad result will be getting no holy
water and/or getting no unholy water.  The probability of getting no
holy water from n flasks is (3/4)^n, and the probability of getting no
unholy water is also (3/4)^n.  The probability of getting either of
these results is the sum of their probabilities minus the probability
that both occur.  If both occur, all the water stayed uncursed and
this has a (1/2)^n probability.

Thus the chance of a good result, getting both holy water and unholy
water from a single scroll, is 1-2*(3/4)^n+(1/2)^n.  Here is a table
